Most commonly asked INTERVIEW QUESTIONS

DIFFERENCE BETWEEN ADD and COPY 

🧱 1️⃣ ADD vs COPY — both put files inside the Docker image

Both ADD and COPY are used to move files from your local machine → into the image.

⸻

🪄 2️⃣ COPY – Simple and clean

👉 COPY just copies files/folders from your system to the image.



📘 Syntax:
  

COPY source destination

📦 Example:

COPY . /app

It copies everything from your current folder into /app inside the image.
🧠 Use COPY for normal file copying — nothing fancy.

🧩 3️⃣ ADD – COPY + Extra Magic

👉 ADD can do everything COPY does, plus:
	1.	It can extract compressed files (.tar, .gz, .bz2) automatically.
	2.	It can download files from a URL (http/https) directly.

📘 Example 1 (auto extract):

ADD app.tar.gz /app

📘 Example 2 (from internet):

ADD https://lnkd.in/g7wT5JRU /app/

🌐 It downloads the file straight from the web.

🧠 5️⃣ Easy Memory Trick

🔹 C in COPY = Clean & Clear
🔹 A in ADD = Advanced features (extract + URL)
